The bit-map flag's clock-domain constraint needs -from, for the PlutoSky R2

Patch 0009 against the R2's constraint file, which patch 0006 for the R2 left
with different context lines. The change is 0009's own.

Replaces firmware/patches/0009 on --rev r2 (same file name).

diff --git a/hdl/projects/pluto/system_constr.xdc b/hdl/projects/pluto/system_constr.xdc
index a299a3d5..5423099d 100755
--- a/hdl/projects/pluto/system_constr.xdc
+++ b/hdl/projects/pluto/system_constr.xdc
@@ -112,10 +112,19 @@ set_property -dict {PACKAGE_PIN M22 IOSTANDARD LVCMOS25 PULLTYPE PULLDOWN} [get_
 # two synchroniser flops close enough together for metastability to settle,
 # without pretending the launch edge means anything.
 #
+# Both ends must be named (patch 0009). "set_max_delay -datapath_only" with
+# only -to is an error (Constraints 18-540, "requires -from to be
+# non-empty"), and in an .xdc that error drops the line without a word in the
+# build log. To see that the limit is really applied, open the routed design
+# and run
+#   report_timing -to [get_cells -hier *flag_m_reg]
+# The requirement must read "(MaxDelay Path 4.000ns)", not two clock edges.
+#
 # Written as a single command: an .xdc is a restricted Tcl dialect and "if" is
 # NOT one of the commands it accepts.
 set_max_delay -datapath_only 4.000 \
-  -to [get_pins -quiet -hier -filter {NAME =~ *tx_bitmap*flag_m_reg/D}]
+  -from [get_cells -quiet -hier -filter {NAME =~ *up_dac_gpio_out_int_reg*}] \
+  -to   [get_cells -quiet -hier -filter {NAME =~ *tx_bitmap*flag_m_reg}]
 
 
 set_property  -dict {PACKAGE_PIN  V10  IOSTANDARD LVCMOS25  PULLTYPE PULLUP} [get_ports spi_csn]
